.TH QUARTERDECK 1 "October 19, 2026" "quarterdeck" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
quarterdeck \- local orchestration board for coding agents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quarterdeck
.RI [ --browser | --desktop ]
.RI [ --host " " ip ]
.RI [ --port " " number|auto ]
.RI [ --no-open ]
.RI [ --no-native-ui ]
.RI [ --skip-shutdown-cleanup ]
.br
.B quarterdeck hooks
.RI " " ingest|notify
.RI " " [ options ]
.br
.B quarterdeck desktop
.RI " " install|status|uninstall
.RI " " [ options ]
.br
.B quarterdeck recover
.RI [ --confirm-stopped ]
.br
.B quarterdeck backup
.RI " " create|list|restore
.RI " " [ options ]
.br
.B quarterdeck diagnostics
.RI " " list|status|doctor|capture|watch|record|mark
.RI " " [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B quarterdeck
opens the installed desktop app on supported local graphical Macs, or starts
the local runtime and browser UI elsewhere. When launched inside a Git
repository, it opens that repository's indexed workspace. When launched
outside Git, it starts without an active workspace or uses an indexed project.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --browser
Open browser mode explicitly. Runtime options and headless environments also
select this mode.
Launch-mode flags cannot be combined with subcommands.
.TP
.B --desktop
Validate the installed macOS app and request native launch.
Cannot be combined with browser-runtime flags or subcommands.
A supported global npm installation installs the matching app; launch never
downloads it.
.TP
.B --host <ip>
Bind the runtime to an IP address. The default is 127.0.0.1.
.TP
.B --port <number|auto>
Bind to a port from 1 through 65535, or select an available port
automatically.
.TP
.B --no-open
Do not open the browser automatically.
.TP
.B --no-native-ui
Disable integrations that launch or interact with host-native UI.
.TP
.B --skip-shutdown-cleanup
Skip graceful shutdown cleanup, including session marking and orphan-process
cleanup. Intended for controlled testing and recovery only.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show help text and exit.
.TP
.B -v, --version
Show the version and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B desktop install [--from <app-path>] [--replace-owner]
Install the matching published macOS app without launching it,
or explicitly import a local app candidate.
Native self-updates are disabled for npm-managed copies.
Replacement uses a temporary backup and journal. Quit the running app and
retry; installation never kills sessions.
Use --replace-owner explicitly when changing the owning checkout or npm
prefix.
.TP
.B desktop status [--json]
Report app, npm owner, and incomplete or mismatched installation state.
With --json, print one JSON object and exit unsuccessfully unless the pair is
ready with no pending work.
.TP
.B desktop uninstall
Remove the owned app before npm uninstall. Preserve projects, sessions, and
runtime data.
.TP
.B hooks ingest [payload]
Ingest an agent hook event into a running Quarterdeck instance. The payload
may be supplied as an argument or on standard input. Hook adapters can also
provide structured fields with options including
.BR --source ,
.BR --activity-text ,
.BR --tool-name ,
.BR --tool-input-summary ,
.BR --final-message ,
.BR --hook-event-name ,
.BR --notification-type ,
.BR --session-id ,
.BR --session-instance-id ,
.BR --turn-id ,
.BR --tool-use-id ,
.BR --transcript-path ,
and
.BR --metadata-base64 .
.TP
.B hooks notify [payload]
Best-effort variant of
.BR "hooks ingest" .
It accepts the same hook fields and does not fail the calling agent when
delivery is unavailable.
.TP
.B recover [--confirm-stopped]
Inspect saved process evidence after an unconfirmed shutdown. Stop any
remaining
agents or detached background commands before passing
.BR --confirm-stopped .
Confirmation permits recovery of the inspected prior history on this boot;
it does not prove detached commands exited. A live runtime, live saved
process,
or unreadable evidence blocks recovery. Saved projects, task work, and
sessions
are preserved. No processes are killed. Reopen Quarterdeck after confirmation.
.TP
.B backup create
Create a manual snapshot of Quarterdeck state. The Quarterdeck runtime must
not be running.
.TP
.B backup list
List available state backups.
.TP
.B backup restore [backup]
Restore a named backup directory, an explicit backup path, or the most recent
backup when omitted. The Quarterdeck server must not be running.
.TP
.B diagnostics list
List active and recently retained runtime instances.
.TP
.B diagnostics status
Show recorder and journal health for a selected runtime.
.TP
.B diagnostics doctor
Run read-only subsystem checks. Use
.B --request-browser
to request a fresh metadata-only browser snapshot and
.B --fail-on-error
to return exit status 5 when an error-severity finding exists.
.TP
.B diagnostics capture
Write a canonical local bundle containing the correlated JSONL timeline,
findings, bounded snapshots, and a hashed manifest. Use
.B --output
to select a new output directory.
.TP
.B diagnostics watch
Watch bounded records for a limited duration. Use
.B --jsonl
for one JSON object per line.
.TP
.B diagnostics record
Start, inspect, or stop an automatically expiring deep-recording window.
Recording can be scoped by project, task, and category and is capped at 15
minutes.
.TP
.B diagnostics mark <message>
Add a bounded correlation marker to the diagnostic timeline.
.PP
Diagnostic selection commands accept options for a specific runtime instance
and scoped project, task, session, operation, source, level, event, and time
range. Use each subcommand's
.B --help
for the complete option set.
.PP
The lightweight metadata-only flight recorder starts automatically. Deep
recording remains content-safe and does not enable terminal transcripts or Git
diffs. Bundles are private local directories and are never uploaded
automatically.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Open Quarterdeck in the default launch mode:
.B quarterdeck
.TP
Start without browser or host-native integrations:
.B quarterdeck --no-open --no-native-ui
.TP
Bind to a custom address and port:
.B quarterdeck --host 0.0.0.0 --port 9000
.TP
Create and list state backups:
.B quarterdeck backup create
.br
.B quarterdeck backup list
.TP
Capture current diagnostic evidence:
.B quarterdeck diagnostics capture --request-browser
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful execution.
.TP
.B 1
Command or runtime operation failed.
.TP
.B 5
.B diagnostics doctor --fail-on-error
found an error-severity issue.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR npm (1)
